<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- DEVELOPMENT: deliberately EMPTY.

       Measured on macOS 26.5.2, isolated one entitlement at a time:

         no entitlements               -> app LAUNCHES
         keychain-access-groups        -> launchd REFUSES to spawn it
                                          (RBSRequestErrorDomain 5, POSIX 163)

       Ad-hoc signing (`codesign --sign -`) cannot satisfy an entitlement that
       needs a team identifier, and rather than being ignored the entitlement
       makes the app un-launchable. So a dev build must carry NONE.

       The consequence is already designed for: CredentialVault probes what the
       keychain actually honours and runs `deviceUnlockedOnly`, saying so at the
       moment the user is asked to save a password (ADR 0007). The vault works;
       it just is not Touch ID gated until there is a real signing identity.

       The full set is in Pane-release.entitlements. Build with
       PANE_RELEASE=1 ./Scripts/bundle.sh once you have an identity. -->
</dict>
</plist>
